{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"home-assistant","name":"Home Assistant","version":"0.1.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":[],"author":"andrearicci93","description":"A Home Assistant card in Vetro's Control center for lights, switches, scenes and scripts. Talks only to the Home Assistant address you set (REST API).","main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Home Assistant"},"controlCenter":{"label":"Home Assistant"}},"files":{"README.md":"# Home Assistant\n\nA Vetro Shard that adds a **Home Assistant card to the Control center** (Down on the launcher's apps row): up to seven\nentities you chose, each with its state (\"Living room · on\"). OK on a row switches it. A page in the Vetro dashboard\nsets it up. It is also the example Shard for the Control center card API.\n\nThis is not Vetro's own Home Assistant connection (MQTT, in the dashboard). That one publishes the TV to Home Assistant;\nthis Shard goes the other way and lets the TV's remote control things in your home.\n\n## What it needs\n\n- **Vetro 0.7.0 or later** for the card. On older versions the Shard loads and its page works, but there is no card.\n- The Control center on: **Vetro UI → Launcher → Control center**, switch **Home Assistant** on (it is off until you do; at most three cards in all).\n- A Home Assistant the TV can reach, and a **long-lived access token**: in Home Assistant, your profile → Security → Long-lived access tokens.\n  Use the server's IP address (`http://192.168.1.20:8123`): a name ending in `.local` often does not resolve on the TV.\n  `https://` works only if the TV trusts the certificate.\n\n## Setting it up\n\n1. Switch the Shard on in **Vetro Shards**, then open its **Home Assistant** page.\n2. Enter the address and the token, **Save and test**. The page reads your entities from Home Assistant.\n3. **Add** up to seven entities, name them, put them in order, **Save the card**.\n\n## What the card does\n\n| Entity | The row shows | OK |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `light`, `switch`, `fan`, `input_boolean` | its state: `on`, `off`, `unavailable` | turns it off if the row says `on`, on otherwise |\n| `scene`, `script` | `Scene`, `Script` | runs it |\n| `button`, `input_button` | `Button` | presses it |\n\n- OK uses the state the row showed (`turn_on` or `turn_off`, never Home Assistant's `toggle`), so a press after a stale read cannot flip the entity back. The row changes at once to what Home Assistant answers.\n- The card is read each time the Control center opens: one call per entity that has a state, never the whole list. If Home Assistant does not answer, the card says why (**HA did not answer**, **Token refused**, **HA address not found**) and the next opening tries again.\n- **Left out on purpose:** locks, covers (garage doors), alarm panels and anything else that opens or disarms something. A remote-control key press should not do that. A script or scene you add runs with the token's full rights, so choose them with that in mind.\n\n## Permissions\n\nNone. It runs no command on the TV.\n\n## Network\n\nOnly the Home Assistant address you set, over HTTP or HTTPS, with your token in the `Authorization` header:\n\n| Request | When |\n| --- | --- |\n| `GET /api/states/<entity_id>` | the Control center opens (one per chosen entity that has a state), and the first press on a row not shown yet |\n| `POST /api/services/<domain>/<service>` with `{\"entity_id\": …}` | OK on a row: `turn_on`, `turn_off` or `press` |\n| `GET /api/states` | only when you open the page or press **Save and test**, to list the entities you can add |\n\nNothing else, and no other host. The address cannot carry a user name or password.\n\n## Data it keeps\n\n`config.json` in the Shard's folder on the TV (Vetro's `ctx.config`, kept across updates): the address, the **token in clear text**, and the\nentities with the names you gave them. The page never gets the token back, the Shard's status does not show it, and **a new address forgets the\nold token** so it cannot be sent somewhere else by changing the address. Anyone who can read the TV's files, or who is a paired device of Vetro, can reach it:\nuse a token made for this, and delete it in Home Assistant if you remove the Shard. Removing the Shard in Vetro deletes the file.\n\n## Tested\n\nAgainst a fake Home Assistant: `tests/home-assistant.test.cjs` (slow answers, `401`, broken JSON, more than seven entities, odd ids, an unknown row, the setup\nroutes) and, by hand, `tests/manual/home-assistant-in-vetro-host.cjs <vetro repo>`, which installs the bundle in Vetro's own plugin host (`plugin-host.js`, commit `f1b48f6`) and\nchecks what the card shows after the host's limits, timeouts and cleaning. The network code also ran on Node 4.4.7, 12 and 22. The author also tried the card on a real TV\nwith a real Home Assistant, through the whole chain (the launcher, the Vetro service, this Shard).\n","ha.js":"'use strict';\n// The Home Assistant side of the Shard: the address, one small HTTP client for HA's REST API, and the table of what the card may\n// switch. Plain ES5 (Node 4.4 on older TVs): no URL global, no Buffer.from, no Array.prototype.includes, no Promise.prototype.finally.\n// Nothing here keeps a timer after a request ends, and abortAll() ends every request that is still open.\n\nvar http = require('http');\nvar https = require('https');\nvar urlLib = require('url');\n\n// What the card may switch, by HA domain. \"switch\" kinds go on or off (turn_on / turn_off, never HA's toggle: a toggle after a stale read\n// would flip the entity back). \"run\" kinds are fired and keep no state. Locks, covers (garage doors) and alarm panels are left out on\n// purpose: a remote-control key press must not open a door.\nvar DOMAINS = {\n    light: { kind: 'switch' },\n    switch: { kind: 'switch' },\n    input_boolean: { kind: 'switch' },\n    fan: { kind: 'switch' },\n    scene: { kind: 'run', service: 'turn_on', value: 'Scene' },\n    script: { kind: 'run', service: 'turn_on', value: 'Script' },\n    button: { kind: 'run', service: 'press', value: 'Button' },\n    input_button: { kind: 'run', service: 'press', value: 'Button' }\n};\n\nvar ENTITY_RE = /^([a-z_]+)\\.[a-z0-9_]+$/;\nvar ID_MAX = 40;            // the longest row id the Control center takes\nvar NAME_MAX = 40;          // the longest row label the Control center takes\nvar MAX_ENTITIES = 7;       // the Control center shows 7 rows at most\nvar TOKEN_RE = /^[\\x21-\\x7e]{1,2048}$/;\n\n// \"192.168.1.20:8123\", \"http://homeassistant:8123\" or \"https://ha.example.org/sub\": {protocol, hostname, port, base} or null. No credentials\n// in the address, no query, no other scheme.\nfunction parseAddress(text) {\n    if (typeof text !== 'string') return null;\n    var t = text.replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, '');\n    if (!t || t.length > 200) return null;\n    if (t.indexOf('://') < 0) t = 'http://' + t;\n    var u;\n    try { u = urlLib.parse(t); } catch (e) { return null; }\n    if (!u || (u.protocol !== 'http:' && u.protocol !== 'https:') || !u.hostname || u.auth || u.search || u.hash) return null;\n    if (/[^A-Za-z0-9.:_\\-\\[\\]]/.test(u.hostname)) return null;\n    var port = u.port ? parseInt(u.port, 10) : (u.protocol === 'https:' ? 443 : 80);\n    if (!(port > 0 && port < 65536)) return null;\n    var base = (u.pathname || '').replace(/\\/+$/, '');\n    if (/[^A-Za-z0-9._~\\-\\/]/.test(base)) return null;\n    return { protocol: u.protocol, hostname: u.hostname, port: port, base: base, text: u.protocol + '//' + (u.hostname.indexOf(':') >= 0 ? '[' + u.hostname + ']' : u.hostname) + ':' + port + base };\n}\n\nfunction validToken(t) { return typeof t === 'string' && TOKEN_RE.test(t); }\n\n// The id of an entity the card can switch: \"light.living_room\". Null for anything else (unknown domain, too long for a row id).\nfunction entityDomain(id) {\n    if (typeof id !== 'string' || id.length > ID_MAX) return null;\n    var m = ENTITY_RE.exec(id);\n    return m && DOMAINS[m[1]] && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(DOMAINS, m[1]) ? m[1] : null;\n}\n\nfunction plain(text, max) {\n    var t = String(text == null ? '' : text).replace(/[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f-\\u009f\\u2028\\u2029]+/g, ' ').replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, '');\n    return t.length > max ? t.slice(0, max).replace(/\\s+$/, '') : t;\n}\n\n// A short sentence for what went wrong, for the card and the page: no address, no token.\nfunction reasonOf(e) {\n    if (!e) return 'HA did not answer';\n    if (e.reason) return e.reason;\n    var c = e.code;\n    if (c === 'ENOTFOUND' || c === 'EAI_AGAIN') return 'HA address not found';\n    if (c && /CERT|SELF_SIGNED|UNABLE_TO_VERIFY|ERR_TLS/.test(c)) return 'HA certificate not trusted';\n    return 'HA did not answer';\n}\n\nfunction fail(reason, status) { var e = new Error(reason); e.reason = reason; e.status = status || 0; return e; }\n\nfunction Client(getConfig) {\n    this.getConfig = getConfig;\n    this.open = [];            // requests under way: stop() aborts them\n}\n\n// request(method, path, body, ms, maxBytes) -> Promise of {status, json}. Always settles within ms (the timer is cleared as soon as it does).\n// Rejects with an Error whose .reason is short readable text. Never throws.\nClient.prototype.request = function (method, path, body, ms, maxBytes) {\n    var self = this;\n    return new Promise(function (resolve, reject) {\n        var cfg = self.getConfig(), addr = parseAddress(cfg.url);\n        if (!addr) return reject(fail('Home Assistant address not set'));\n        if (!validToken(cfg.token)) return reject(fail('Access token not set'));\n        var payload = body == null ? null : JSON.stringify(body);\n        var done = false, timer = null, req = null;\n        function finish(err, value) {\n            if (done) return;\n            done = true;\n            if (timer) clearTimeout(timer);\n            var i = self.open.indexOf(abort);\n            if (i >= 0) self.open.splice(i, 1);\n            if (err) reject(err); else resolve(value);\n        }\n        function abort() { finish(fail('HA did not answer')); try { if (req) req.abort(); } catch (e) { /* already closed */ } }\n        self.open.push(abort);\n        timer = setTimeout(abort, ms);\n        try {\n            var headers = { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + cfg.token, Accept: 'application/json' };\n            if (payload != null) { headers['Content-Type'] = 'application/json'; headers['Content-Length'] = Buffer.byteLength(payload); }\n            req = (addr.protocol === 'https:' ? https : http).request({\n                method: method, hostname: addr.hostname, port: addr.port, path: addr.base + path, headers: headers, agent: false\n            }, function (res) {\n                var chunks = [], size = 0;\n                res.setEncoding('utf8');\n                res.on('data', function (c) {\n                    size += c.length;\n                    if (size > maxBytes) { finish(fail('HA answer is too large')); try { req.abort(); } catch (e) { /* closed */ } return; }\n                    chunks.push(c);\n                });\n                res.on('error', function (e) { finish(fail(reasonOf(e))); });\n                res.on('aborted', function () { finish(fail('HA did not answer')); });\n                res.on('end', function () {\n                    var s = res.statusCode;\n                    if (s === 401 || s === 403) return finish(fail('Token refused', s));\n                    if (s === 404) return finish(fail('Not found', s));\n                    if (s >= 300 && s < 400) return finish(fail('HA redirected: use its final address', s));\n                    if (s < 200 || s >= 300) return finish(fail('HA answered ' + s, s));\n                    var json = null, text = chunks.join('');\n                    if (text) { try { json = JSON.parse(text); } catch (e) { return finish(fail('HA sent something unreadable', s)); } }\n                    finish(null, { status: s, json: json });\n                });\n            });\n            req.on('error', function (e) { finish(fail(reasonOf(e))); });\n            if (payload != null) req.write(payload);\n            req.end();\n        } catch (e) { finish(fail(reasonOf(e))); }\n    });\n};\n\nClient.prototype.abortAll = function () {\n    var list = this.open.slice();\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) { try { list[i](); } catch (e) { /* the request is gone anyway */ } }\n    this.open = [];\n};\n\nmodule.exports = {\n    DOMAINS: DOMAINS, ID_MAX: ID_MAX, NAME_MAX: NAME_MAX, MAX_ENTITIES: MAX_ENTITIES,\n    parseAddress: parseAddress, validToken: validToken, entityDomain: entityDomain, plain: plain, reasonOf: reasonOf,\n    Client: Client\n};\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// Home Assistant: a Vetro Shard that adds one card to the launcher's Control center (Down on the apps row) and a page in the dashboard\n// to set it up. The card lists up to 7 entities you chose (lights, switches, scenes, scripts, buttons) with their state; OK on a row\n// switches it. It talks only to the Home Assistant address you set, through HA's REST API with a long-lived access token.\n// Plain ES5 (var, function): older TVs run Node 4.4. The launcher never runs this code: Vetro asks card() and cardSelect() for it.\n//\n// Rows are never ticked. The Control center ignores OK on a ticked row, and a light you can only turn on is no use: the state is\n// written in the row's value (\"Living room · on\") and OK sends turn_on or turn_off for the opposite of what the row shows.\n\nvar fs = require('fs');\nvar path = require('path');\nvar ha = require('./ha.js');\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var READ_MS = 2500;            // card(): the host gives up after 3 s\n    var ACTION_MS = 8500;          // cardSelect(): the host gives up after 10 s, in all (one read at most, then the service call)\n    var MAX_BODY = 16 * 1024;\n\n    var cfg = null;                // {url, token, entities: [{id, name}]}, read from ctx.config\n    var shown = null;              // what the card last showed: {rows: [...], states: {id: 'on'|'off'|...}}\n    var lastError = null;\n    var client = new ha.Client(function () { return conf(); });\n\n    function cleanEntities(list) {\n        var out = [], seen = {};\n        if (!Array.isArray(list)) return out;\n        for (var i = 0; i < list.length && out.length < ha.MAX_ENTITIES; i++) {\n            var e = list[i];\n            if (!e || typeof e !== 'object' || !ha.entityDomain(e.id) || seen[e.id]) continue;\n            seen[e.id] = true;\n            out.push({ id: e.id, name: ha.plain(e.name, ha.NAME_MAX) });\n        }\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    function readConfig() {\n        var raw = null;\n        try { raw = ctx.config.get(); } catch (e) { raw = null; }\n        if (!raw || typeof raw !== 'object') raw = {};\n        return { url: typeof raw.url === 'string' ? raw.url : '', token: typeof raw.token === 'string' ? raw.token : '', entities: cleanEntities(raw.entities) };\n    }\n    function conf() { return cfg || (cfg = readConfig()); }\n    function configured() { var c = conf(); return !!ha.parseAddress(c.url) && ha.validToken(c.token); }\n    function find(id) { var l = conf().entities; for (var i = 0; i < l.length; i++) if (l[i].id === id) return l[i]; return null; }\n\n    function json(res, body, code) {\n        res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n    }\n    function html() {\n        var places = [path.join(__dirname, 'ui.html'), path.join(ctx.dir || '', 'ui.html')];\n        for (var i = 0; i < places.length; i++) { try { return fs.readFileSync(places[i], 'utf8'); } catch (e) { /* next */ } }\n        return '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"><body style=\"font:16px system-ui;margin:24px\">ui.html is missing from this Shard.</body>';\n    }\n    function readBody(req, cb) {\n        var chunks = [], size = 0, done = false;\n        req.on('data', function (c) { size += c.length; if (size > MAX_BODY) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(new Error('Request too large')); } return; } chunks.push(c); });\n        req.on('end', function () {\n            if (done) return;\n            done = true;\n            var p;\n            try { p = JSON.parse(Buffer.concat(chunks).toString('utf8') || '{}'); } catch (e) { return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON')); }\n            if (!p || typeof p !== 'object' || Array.isArray(p)) return cb(new Error('Invalid JSON'));\n            cb(null, p);\n        });\n        req.on('error', function (e) { if (!done) { done = true; cb(e); } });\n    }\n\n    // ---- the card --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    function rowsOf(c, results) {\n        var rows = [], states = {}, switches = 0, on = 0;\n        for (var i = 0; i < c.entities.length; i++) {\n            var e = c.entities[i], def = ha.DOMAINS[ha.entityDomain(e.id)], r = results[i];\n            if (def.kind === 'run') { rows.push({ id: e.id, label: e.name || e.id, value: def.value, ticked: false }); continue; }\n            switches++;\n            var label = e.name || (r.state && r.state.attributes && ha.plain(r.state.attributes.friendly_name, ha.NAME_MAX)) || e.id, value;\n            if (r.state && typeof r.state.state === 'string') {\n                value = ha.plain(r.state.state, 24);\n                states[e.id] = value;\n                if (value === 'on') on++;\n            } else value = r.err && r.err.status === 404 ? 'missing' : 'n/a';\n            rows.push({ id: e.id, label: label, value: value, ticked: false });\n        }\n        return { rows: rows, states: states, note: switches ? on + ' of ' + switches + ' on' : '' };\n    }\n\n    // One GET per chosen entity that has a state, all at once (never /api/states: on a real HA that is thousands of entities).\n    function card() {\n        var c = conf();\n        if (!configured()) return { rows: [], note: 'Set the Home Assistant address in the Shard page', choosable: false };\n        if (!c.entities.length) return { rows: [], note: 'Choose entities in the Shard page', choosable: false };\n        var reads = c.entities.map(function (e) {\n            if (ha.DOMAINS[ha.entityDomain(e.id)].kind === 'run') return Promise.resolve({});\n            return client.request('GET', '/api/states/' + e.id, null, READ_MS, 64 * 1024).then(\n                function (r) { return { state: r.json }; },\n                function (err) { return { err: err }; });\n        });\n        return Promise.all(reads).then(function (results) {\n            var asked = 0, failed = [], i;\n            for (i = 0; i < results.length; i++) {\n                if (ha.DOMAINS[ha.entityDomain(c.entities[i].id)].kind === 'run') continue;\n                asked++;\n                if (results[i].err && results[i].err.status !== 404) failed.push(results[i].err);\n            }\n            if (asked && failed.length === asked) {\n                var worst = failed[0];\n                for (i = 0; i < failed.length; i++) if (failed[i].status === 401 || failed[i].status === 403) worst = failed[i];\n                lastError = ha.reasonOf(worst);\n                throw new Error(lastError);\n            }\n            lastError = null;\n            var built = rowsOf(c, results);\n            shown = { rows: built.rows, states: built.states };\n            return { rows: built.rows, note: built.note, choosable: true };\n        });\n    }\n\n    function shownRows() { return shown ? { rows: shown.rows.map(function (r) { return { id: r.id, label: r.label, value: r.value, ticked: false }; }) } : {}; }\n\n    // A press that did not work: the card stays as it was, with a note. The rows go back too, so the host does not read the card again\n    // (with Home Assistant down that read would add 2.5 s to an action that already took 8.5, past the launcher's 12 s).\n    function refused(note) { var out = shownRows(); out.ok = false; out.note = note; return out; }\n    function noteFor(err) { lastError = ha.reasonOf(err); return refused(lastError); }\n\n    // OK on a row. Never throws and never rejects: a failure is {ok: false, note}, so the card stays and says why.\n    function cardSelect(rowId) {\n        try {\n            var ent = find(rowId);\n            if (!ent || !configured()) return refused(ent ? 'Set the Home Assistant address in the Shard page' : 'Not one of the chosen entities');\n            var domain = ha.entityDomain(ent.id), def = ha.DOMAINS[domain], started = Date.now();\n            var call = function (service, budget) {\n                return client.request('POST', '/api/services/' + domain + '/' + service, { entity_id: ent.id }, Math.max(1500, budget), 256 * 1024);\n            };\n            if (def.kind === 'run') {\n                return call(def.service, ACTION_MS).then(function () { lastError = null; var s = shownRows(); s.ok = true; return s; }, noteFor);\n            }\n            // The state the row showed decides what OK means: the user pressed \"turn this off\" because the row said \"on\". A fresh read\n            // is only for a row nobody has shown yet.\n            var known = shown && shown.states[ent.id];\n            var state = known ? Promise.resolve(known) : client.request('GET', '/api/states/' + ent.id, null, READ_MS, 64 * 1024).then(function (r) {\n                return r.json && typeof r.json.state === 'string' ? r.json.state : 'unknown';\n            });\n            return state.then(function (now) {\n                if (now === 'unavailable') return refused((ent.name || ent.id) + ' is unavailable');\n                var want = now === 'on' ? 'off' : 'on';\n                return call('turn_' + want, ACTION_MS - (Date.now() - started)).then(function (r) {\n                    // HA answers with the states that changed during the call; if the entity is not among them (a slow device), expect the new one.\n                    var after = want, list = r.json;\n                    if (Array.isArray(list)) {\n                        for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n                            if (list[i] && list[i].entity_id === ent.id && typeof list[i].state === 'string') { after = ha.plain(list[i].state, 24); break; }\n                        }\n                    }\n                    lastError = null;\n                    if (!shown) return { ok: true };\n                    shown.states[ent.id] = after;\n                    for (var j = 0; j < shown.rows.length; j++) if (shown.rows[j].id === ent.id) shown.rows[j].value = after;\n                    var out = shownRows();\n                    out.ok = true;\n                    return out;\n                }, noteFor);\n            }, noteFor);\n        } catch (e) { return refused(ha.reasonOf(e)); }\n    }\n\n    // ---- the page --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    function publicConfig() {\n        var c = conf();\n        return { url: c.url, hasToken: !!c.token, entities: c.entities, max: ha.MAX_ENTITIES };\n    }\n\n    // Applies what the page sent. Only the keys that are there change. The token is never sent back to the page, and it does not follow\n    // the address: a new address without a new token forgets the old one.\n    function applyConfig(p) {\n        var cur = conf(), next = { url: cur.url, token: cur.token, entities: cur.entities }, i;\n        var typed = typeof p.token === 'string' ? p.token.replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, '') : '';\n        if (p.url !== undefined) {\n            if (typeof p.url !== 'string') return { error: 'The address must be text' };\n            var text = p.url.replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, '');\n            if (!text) { next.url = ''; next.token = ''; }\n            else {\n                var addr = ha.parseAddress(text), old = ha.parseAddress(cur.url);\n                if (!addr) return { error: 'Not an address: use http://192.168.1.20:8123 (no user name or password in it)' };\n                if (!old || old.text !== addr.text) next.token = '';\n                next.url = addr.text;\n            }\n        }\n        if (p.clearToken === true) next.token = '';\n        if (typed) {\n            if (!ha.validToken(typed)) return { error: 'That is not an access token (letters and digits, no spaces)' };\n            next.token = typed;\n        }\n        if (p.entities !== undefined) {\n            if (!Array.isArray(p.entities) || p.entities.length > ha.MAX_ENTITIES) return { error: 'The card holds at most ' + ha.MAX_ENTITIES + ' entities' };\n            var seen = {}, list = [];\n            for (i = 0; i < p.entities.length; i++) {\n                var e = p.entities[i];\n                if (!e || typeof e !== 'object' || !ha.entityDomain(e.id)) return { error: String(e && e.id).slice(0, 60) + ' cannot be on the card (not a light, switch, fan, scene, script or button, or longer than ' + ha.ID_MAX + ' characters)' };\n                if (seen[e.id]) return { error: e.id + ' is listed twice' };\n                seen[e.id] = true;\n                list.push({ id: e.id, name: ha.plain(e.name, ha.NAME_MAX) });\n            }\n            next.entities = list;\n        }\n        try { ctx.config.set(next); } catch (err) { return { error: 'Could not save: ' + ha.plain(err && err.message, 80) }; }\n        var forgot = !!cur.token && !next.token;\n        cfg = next;\n        shown = null;\n        return { ok: true, tokenForgotten: forgot };\n    }\n\n    // What the picker offers: every entity of a supported type, from one /api/states call (the only place that reads them all).\n    function listEntities(res) {\n        if (!configured()) return json(res, { error: 'Save the address and the access token first' }, 400);\n        client.request('GET', '/api/states', null, 9000, 12 * 1024 * 1024).then(function (r) {\n            var out = [], list = Array.isArray(r.json) ? r.json : [];\n            for (var i = 0; i < list.length && out.length < 800; i++) {\n                var s = list[i], id = s && s.entity_id;\n                if (typeof id !== 'string') continue;\n                var m = /^([a-z_]+)\\./.exec(id), def = m && Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(ha.DOMAINS, m[1]) ? ha.DOMAINS[m[1]] : null;\n                if (!def) continue;\n                var name = ha.plain(s.attributes && s.attributes.friendly_name, ha.NAME_MAX) || id.slice(0, ha.NAME_MAX);\n                out.push({ id: id.slice(0, 80), name: name, state: ha.plain(s.state, 24), kind: def.kind, usable: !!ha.entityDomain(id) });\n            }\n            out.sort(function (a, b) { return a.name.toLowerCase() < b.name.toLowerCase() ? -1 : a.name.toLowerCase() > b.name.toLowerCase() ? 1 : 0; });\n            lastError = null;\n            json(res, { entities: out });\n        }).then(null, function (err) {\n            lastError = ha.reasonOf(err);\n            if (!res.headersSent) json(res, { error: lastError }, 502);\n        });\n    }\n\n    return {\n        start: function () { cfg = readConfig(); shown = null; lastError = null; },\n        stop: function () { client.abortAll(); shown = null; },\n\n        // Nothing secret: the dashboard shows this. Not the token, not the full address.\n        status: function () {\n            var a = ha.parseAddress(conf().url);\n            return { configured: configured(), host: a ? a.hostname + ':' + a.port : null, entities: conf().entities.length, error: lastError };\n        },\n\n        card: card,\n        cardSelect: cardSelect,\n\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n                res.end(html());\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'config' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, publicConfig()); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'config' && req.method === 'POST') {\n                readBody(req, function (err, p) {\n                    if (err) return json(res, { error: err.message }, 400);\n                    var r = applyConfig(p);\n                    if (r.error) return json(res, { error: r.error }, 400);\n                    var out = publicConfig();\n                    out.tokenForgotten = r.tokenForgotten;\n                    json(res, out);\n                });\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'entities' && req.method === 'GET') { listEntities(res); return true; }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n","ui.html":"<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\"><title>Home Assistant</title>\n<style>\n:root{--bg:#080f23;--surface:#101c35;--raised:#192943;--border:#344360;--text:#f5f8ff;--muted:#aab8d1;--accent:#8fbaff;--action:#123bb5;--ok:#7fcba0;--danger:#ef8a80}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme:light){:root{--bg:#f5f8ff;--surface:#fff;--raised:#eef2fb;--border:#c9d3e6;--text:#0b1430;--muted:#4a5878;--accent:#123bb5;--ok:#1e7a4a;--danger:#b3261e}}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;padding:16px;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font:14px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}\n.panel{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:16px;padding:16px;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:720px}\nh2{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:16px}p{margin:0 0 8px}.note{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}\n.field{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;margin:12px 0 0;max-width:420px}.field span{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}\ninput,button{height:36px;padding:0 12px;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;background:var(--raised);color:inherit;font:inherit}\ninput{width:100%}button{cursor:pointer}button.primary{background:var(--action);border-color:var(--action);color:#f5f8ff;font-weight:600}\nbutton:disabled,input:disabled{opacity:.5;cursor:default}button.small{height:30px;padding:0 10px}\n.row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin:12px 0 0}\nul{list-style:none;margin:12px 0 0;padding:0}li{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:6px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}li:first-child{border-top:0}\nli .main{flex:1;min-width:0}li .main b{display:block;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}li .main small{color:var(--muted)}\nli input{flex:1;min-width:0}.msg{min-height:1.5em;margin-top:12px;font-size:12px}.msg.bad{color:var(--danger)}.msg.good{color:var(--ok)}\n#pick{max-height:320px;overflow:auto}\n</style></head><body>\n\n<div class=\"panel\"><h2>Connection</h2>\n<p class=\"note\">The card talks to this Home Assistant and to nothing else. Use its IP address: a name ending in .local often does not resolve on the TV.</p>\n<label class=\"field\"><span>Home Assistant address</span><input id=\"url\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"http://192.168.1.20:8123\"></label>\n<label class=\"field\"><span id=\"tokenLabel\">Long-lived access token</span><input id=\"token\" type=\"password\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"Paste a token\"></label>\n<p class=\"note\" style=\"margin-top:8px\">Create one in Home Assistant: your profile → Security → Long-lived access tokens. It is kept on the TV and never shown here again.</p>\n<div class=\"row\"><button id=\"save\" class=\"primary\">Save and test</button><button id=\"forget\">Forget the token</button></div>\n<p id=\"connMsg\" class=\"msg\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"panel\"><h2>On the card</h2>\n<p class=\"note\">Up to <span id=\"max\">7</span> entities, in this order. OK on a row in the Control center switches it. Turn the card on in Vetro UI → Launcher → Control center.</p>\n<ul id=\"chosen\"></ul><p id=\"none\" class=\"note\">Nothing chosen yet.</p>\n<div class=\"row\"><button id=\"apply\" class=\"primary\">Save the card</button></div>\n<p id=\"cardMsg\" class=\"msg\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p></div>\n\n<div class=\"panel\"><h2>Add an entity</h2>\n<p class=\"note\">Lights, switches, fans, input booleans, scenes, scripts and buttons. Locks, garage doors and alarms are left out on purpose.</p>\n<label class=\"field\"><span>Search</span><input id=\"search\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" placeholder=\"living, light.kitchen…\"></label>\n<ul id=\"pick\"></ul><p id=\"pickMsg\" class=\"msg\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p></div>\n\n<script>\nvar cfg = { entities: [], max: 7 }, chosen = [], all = [];\nfunction $(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\nfunction el(tag, text, cls) { var e = document.createElement(tag); if (text != null) e.textContent = text; if (cls) e.className = cls; return e; }\nfunction say(id, text, kind) { var e = $(id); e.textContent = text || ''; e.className = 'msg' + (kind ? ' ' + kind : ''); }\nfunction send(body) {\n  return fetch('config', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain' }, body: JSON.stringify(body) })\n    .then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (d) { if (!r.ok) throw new Error(d.error || 'Failed'); return d; }); });\n}\nfunction applyConfig(d, keepChosen) {      // keepChosen: a card list edited and not saved yet survives a change of the connection\n  cfg = d; if (!keepChosen) chosen = d.entities.map(function (e) { return { id: e.id, name: e.name }; });\n  $('url').value = d.url || ''; $('max').textContent = d.max;\n  $('token').value = ''; $('token').placeholder = d.hasToken ? 'A token is saved. Paste a new one to replace it' : 'Paste a token';\n  $('forget').disabled = !d.hasToken; renderChosen(); renderPick();\n}\nfunction renderChosen() {\n  var ul = $('chosen'); ul.innerHTML = ''; $('none').hidden = chosen.length > 0;\n  chosen.forEach(function (c, i) {\n    var li = el('li'), name = el('input'); name.value = c.name; name.maxLength = 40; name.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Name of ' + c.id);\n    name.oninput = function () { c.name = name.value; };\n    var id = el('small', c.id, 'note'); id.style.width = '30%'; id.style.overflow = 'hidden'; id.style.textOverflow = 'ellipsis';\n    var up = el('button', '↑', 'small'), down = el('button', '↓', 'small'), del = el('button', 'Remove', 'small');\n    up.disabled = i === 0; down.disabled = i === chosen.length - 1;\n    up.onclick = function () { chosen.splice(i - 1, 0, chosen.splice(i, 1)[0]); renderChosen(); };\n    down.onclick = function () { chosen.splice(i + 1, 0, chosen.splice(i, 1)[0]); renderChosen(); };\n    del.onclick = function () { chosen.splice(i, 1); renderChosen(); renderPick(); };\n    [name, id, up, down, del].forEach(function (n) { li.appendChild(n); }); ul.appendChild(li);\n  });\n}\nfunction renderPick() {\n  var ul = $('pick'), q = $('search').value.toLowerCase(); ul.innerHTML = '';\n  var taken = {}; chosen.forEach(function (c) { taken[c.id] = true; });\n  var shown = 0;\n  all.forEach(function (e) {\n    if (q && e.name.toLowerCase().indexOf(q) < 0 && e.id.toLowerCase().indexOf(q) < 0) return;\n    if (shown++ >= 60) return;\n    var li = el('li'), main = el('div', null, 'main'), add = el('button', taken[e.id] ? 'Added' : 'Add', 'small');\n    main.appendChild(el('b', e.name)); main.appendChild(el('small', e.id + (e.kind === 'switch' ? ' · ' + e.state : ' · runs when pressed')));\n    add.disabled = !e.usable || taken[e.id] || chosen.length >= cfg.max;\n    if (!e.usable) add.title = 'The id is longer than 40 characters: the Control center cannot take it';\n    add.onclick = function () { chosen.push({ id: e.id, name: e.name }); renderChosen(); renderPick(); };\n    li.appendChild(main); li.appendChild(add); ul.appendChild(li);\n  });\n  if (shown > 60) say('pickMsg', 'Showing 60 of ' + shown + '. Search to narrow it down.');\n  else if (all.length && !shown) say('pickMsg', 'Nothing matches.');\n  else if (!all.length) say('pickMsg', '');\n  else say('pickMsg', '');\n}\nfunction loadEntities() {\n  say('pickMsg', 'Reading Home Assistant…');\n  return fetch('entities').then(function (r) { return r.json().then(function (d) { return { ok: r.ok, d: d }; }); }).then(function (x) {\n    if (!x.ok) { all = []; renderPick(); say('pickMsg', x.d.error || 'Home Assistant did not answer', 'bad'); say('connMsg', x.d.error || 'Home Assistant did not answer', 'bad'); return false; }\n    all = x.d.entities; renderPick(); say('connMsg', 'Connected. ' + all.length + ' entities can go on the card.', 'good'); return true;\n  }).catch(function () { say('pickMsg', 'The TV did not answer', 'bad'); });\n}\n$('search').oninput = renderPick;\n$('save').onclick = function () {\n  var body = { url: $('url').value }, t = $('token').value;\n  if (t) body.token = t;\n  say('connMsg', 'Saving…');\n  send(body).then(function (d) {\n    applyConfig(d, true);\n    if (d.tokenForgotten && !t) { say('connMsg', 'The address changed, so the old token was forgotten. Paste a token for the new one.', 'bad'); return; }\n    if (!d.url) { say('connMsg', 'Address removed.'); all = []; renderPick(); return; }\n    if (!d.hasToken) { say('connMsg', 'Saved. Paste a token to connect.'); return; }\n    return loadEntities();\n  }).catch(function (e) { say('connMsg', e.message, 'bad'); });\n};\n$('forget').onclick = function () { send({ clearToken: true }).then(function (d) { applyConfig(d, true); all = []; renderPick(); say('connMsg', 'Token forgotten.'); }).catch(function (e) { say('connMsg', e.message, 'bad'); }); };\n$('apply').onclick = function () {\n  say('cardMsg', 'Saving…');\n  send({ entities: chosen }).then(function (d) { applyConfig(d); say('cardMsg', 'Saved. The card shows it the next time the Control center opens.', 'good'); }).catch(function (e) { say('cardMsg', e.message, 'bad'); });\n};\nfetch('config').then(function (r) { return r.json(); }).then(function (d) { applyConfig(d); if (d.url && d.hasToken) loadEntities(); else say('connMsg', 'Enter the address and a token to begin.'); })\n  .catch(function () { say('connMsg', 'The TV did not answer', 'bad'); });\n</script></body></html>\n"}}
